cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "agent-security-vet: offline, static security vetting for AI-agent skills, plugins, MCP servers and web content"
abstract: >-
  agent-security-vet is a Claude Code skill (vet-agent-security) plus an offline,
  static scanner written with the Python standard library only. It checks
  third-party agent skills, plugins, MCP servers and repositories before
  installation, checks articles and web pages for hidden prompt injection, and
  audits a browsing-agent setup with benign canary pages. It never executes
  the content it scans. A clean scan is not proof of safety.
authors:
  - name: "agent-security-vet contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/voxmortem/agent-security-vet"
url: "https://github.com/voxmortem/agent-security-vet"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-26
keywords:
  - prompt-injection
  - indirect-prompt-injection
